  "description": "AMENDED SPECIFICATION agreed by email. 19.11.2025\rWorks to a tree in a conservation area: T6137 - Oak - Reduce 17m high tree to approximately 10m AGL. Where possible retain at least 1.5 to 2m of primary branching structure at crown break. 50% Lateral reduction to suitable pruning points reducing a 14m overall spread to 7m OR 3.5m from stem. Deadwood. Reason: Extensive Decay. Hollowed base caused by Grifola fungi spp. VALID Assessment undertaken which indicates a 40% reduction is required, together with PICUS sonic tomographic outputs and microdrill resistance records. The tree is otherwise at risk of stem shear.",
